\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee at 1-mth low,dollar bid by state banks  \b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2006\par 03:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to afternoon)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 17 (Reuters) - The rupee extended losses to a one-month low versus the dollar on Friday, on weakness in the yen and dollar-buying by state banks that traders said could be either on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or corporates.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , through state banks, is suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this week to keep the rupee from strengthening and harming exporter competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 At 13:40 p.m. (0810 GMT), the rupee <INR=IN> stood at 44.4600/4650 per dollar, down about a fifth of a percent from Thursday's close. It weakened as far as 44.47, its lowest level since Jan. 18, according to Reuters data.  \par \par \uc2 "The nationalised banks have definitely been buying dollars," said a trader at a foreign bank in Mumbai. "That could be for the RBI or corporates -- it's hard to tell."  \par \par \uc2 Investors have also been covering short positions on the dollar since the rupee broke through recent ranges on Thursday, accelerating the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 This week's hawkish comments on the U.S. economy from new Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke have refocused attention on the prospect for further U.S. interest rate rises that could tempt investors out of local markets, hurting the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 "The weaker rupee is basically a reaction to the yen but there is also a fear that the Fed will continue to hike rates," said Patrick Aranha, chief dealer at Mizuho in Mumbai.  \par \par \uc2 "Since we broke above 44.30 yesterday, there has been a covering of short positions."  \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds sold a net $13 million worth of Indian shares on Wednesday. It was the second straight day of net selling. Total net buying so far this year is about $1.5 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The yen <JPY=> eased against the dollar on Friday after failing to gain from data showing robust growth in Japan's economy in the final quarter of last year.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   ------------------------------------------------------------\par                  MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060220e22h00050\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
