\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee extends fall to 1-month low vs dollar  \b0\par\par\uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2006\par 03:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, Feb 17 (Reuters) - The rupee extended losses to a one-month low against the dollar on Friday, hurt by a combination of factors such as a soft yen and worries about a possible slowdown of foreign funds into India.  \par \par \uc2  Dollar-buying by state banks that traders said could be either on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or corporates also weighed on the rupee.  \par \par \uc2  A trader at a foreign bank in Mumbai said dollar buying related to demand for oil imports added to rupee weakness.  \par \par \uc2  "There has been huge demand for dollars today," he said. "State banks were buying in the morning and selling in the afternoon. So net-net, there doesn't seem to have been anything specific coming from the RBI."  \par \par \uc2  The rupee fell as far as 44.4975 per dollar, its lowest level since Jan. 18, according to Reuters data. It recovered slightly to close at 44.46/47 per dollar but was still down a quarter of a percent from Thursday's close and 0.6 percent lower on the week.  \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , via state banks, is suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this week to keep the rupee from strengthening and harming exporter competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2  In the past two days the rupee has come under pressure to weaken from another source -- Wednesday's hawkish comments on the U.S. economy from new Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke have renewed worries that rising U.S. interest rates will tempt foreign investors away from local markets.  \par \par \uc2  Foreign demand for Indian stocks has been strong but the pace of inflows has eased off a bit in the past few sessions.  \par \par \uc2  Net buying so far this year has totalled about $1.6 billion and foreign funds bought a net $55.7 million worth of shares on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2  The benchmark BSE index <.BSESN>, however, shed 1.4 percent on Friday. It posted its biggest one-day decline in nearly five weeks -- undermining the rupee.  \par \par \uc2  "The weaker rupee is basically a reaction to the yen but there is also a fear that the Fed will continue to hike rates," said Patrick Aranha, chief dealer at Mizuho in Mumbai.  \par \par \uc2  "Since we broke above 44.30 yesterday, there has been a covering of short positions."  \par \par \uc2  The yen <JPY=> eased against the dollar on Friday after failing to gain from data showing robust growth in Japan's economy in the final quarter of last year.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   ------------------------------------------------------------\par                  MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060220e22h0004y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
