\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee higher but c.bank seen checking gains  \b0\par\par\uc2 464 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2006\par 04:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 14 (Reuters) - The rupee edged higher on Tuesday underpinned by strong foreign investor inflows but dealers said they suspected dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that capped gains in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 A rally in the yen <JPY=> and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar also supported the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee <INR=IN> ended the day at 44.22/2275 per dollar, up 0.12 percent from Monday's close and above a one-week low at about 44.29 per dollar hit that session.  \par \par \uc2 "There is a lot of foreign investor interest in the rupee but nationalised banks have been buying the dollar," said one trader in Mumbai.  \par \par \uc2 "There was a talk that this buying was on behalf of the RBI (Reserve Bank of India) but we don't know for sure."  \par \par \uc2 India's benchmark stock index <.BSESN> hit a new high for a third straight session on Tuesday before retreating slightly. Foreign funds bought net shares worth $138 million on Friday, taking the total to about $1.5 billion so far this year.  \par \par \uc2 But upward pressure on the rupee from foreign inflows has been offset by state banks buying dollars for rupees on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not want a firm rupee to hurt exporter competitiveness and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped weaken the rupee about 0.40 percent from four-month highs hit two weeks ago.  \par \par \uc2 "We have heard that some of the state banks were buying dollars today but we are not sure if this was on corporate demand or on behalf of the RBI," a dealer at a government-owned bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say a rise in \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves suggests \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has increased significantly in the past few weeks.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to $139.98 billion on Feb. 3 from $139.48 a week earlier, data on Friday showed.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee showed little reaction to data showing India's trade deficit narrowed in January to $2.91 billion from $3.3 billion in the same month a year earlier.  \par \par \uc2 "From a near-term perspective, the narrowing in the trade gap is good for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Shuchita Mehta, chief economist India at Standard Chartered Bank.  \par \par \uc2 Attention on Wednesday was expected to turn to new U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke, who testifies to the House Financial Services Committee.  \par \par \uc2 Hawkish comments from Bernanke that reinforce expectations for higher U.S. interest rates could undermine the rupee and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ------------------------------------------------------------\par                  MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060217e22e000a0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal