\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Rupee Ends Up Despite RBI  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Dn  \b0\par\par\uc2 827 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2006\par 13:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee ended higher against the dollar Tuesday as investors sold the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid continued inflows into the local stock market, although \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  led \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited the gains.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at INR44.2050, down from INR44.2350 at the previous close and off its intraday high of INR44.3050.  \par \par \uc2 Foreigners have bought stocks worth $550 million so far this month, following purchases worth $805 million in January, helping the Bombay Stock Exchange to scale the psychological 10000 mark Monday.  \par \par \uc2 However, large dollar purchases by state-run banks acting on behalf of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited the rupee's gains. The RBI has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over the last few sessions, buying the dollar to keep the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating too much.  \par \par \uc2 But they scaled back their purchases later in the session Tuesday, traders said. Dealers estimate that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has mopped up around $1 billion-$1.5 billion in the past few days.  \par \par \uc2 "The rupee has been strengthening in line with the dollar's recent weakness overseas," a trader at a European bank said. "But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been keeping the rupee on a tight leash."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to a new four-month low of INR44.07 against the rupee last week as foreign funds bought into Asia's fastest growing economy after China.  \par \par \uc2 "They have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curtail the rupee's overvaluation against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a trade-weighted basis," said Sundeep Bhandari, regional head, global markets-South Asia in Standard Chartered Bank, India.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained 1.87% against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the start of 2006. Analysts say it is already 8%-9% overvalued in trade-weighted terms.  \par \par \uc2 Indian government bonds ended lower Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set lower-than-expected cutoffs at twin federal bond auctions, suggesting that bond yields may rise in coming weeks.  \par \par \uc2 The actively traded 8.07% bond maturing in 2017 closed down at INR105.28 from INR105.53 previously. Its yield rose three basis points to 7.36%.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier Tuesday, the Reserve Bank of India set a cutoff of INR100.60 on the 7.46% bond maturing in 2017, below the widely expected INR100.70, while the cutoff on the 7.40% paper maturing in 2035 was set at INR97.27, well below market expectations of INR98.50-INR98.80.  \par \par \uc2 "With robust economic growth expectations and liquidity remaining tight, the mood is very bond bearish at the moment," a fund manager said.  \par \par \uc2 The government estimated economic growth in the current fiscal year at 8.1%, fueled by robust consumer demand and rising credit boosting manufacturing and demand for services.  \par \par \uc2 Shrinking banking system liquidity is evident from the bids received by the RBI at its daily repo auctions. It injected funds worth INR149 billion Tuesday, compared with last week's INR115 billion daily average.  \par \par \uc2 In the market for overnight funds, the call money rate ended slightly lower as tepid demand from banks to meet reserve targets was offset by shrinking banking system liquidity. The call money rate closed at 6.90%-7.10% from 7.00%-7.25% at the previous close.  \par \par \uc2 Dollar forward rates fell, tracking lower money market rates. The dollar forward contract maturing in January 2007 ended down at premium of INR0.630 from INR0.640 previously.  \par \par \uc2 Interest rate swaps benchmarked to the Mumbai interbank forward offered rate, or MIFOR, also fell, tracking lower dollar forward rates. The five-year swap slipped to 6.31%-6.36%, compared with 6.39%-6.44% at the previous close.  \par \par \uc2 Overnight indexed swap rates ended higher, tracking higher government bond yields. The five-year swap ended up at 6.72%-6.73% from 6.69%-6.70% at the previous close. [ 07-02-06 1257GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Rupee Vs Dollar Close \par Tuesday          Previous \par INR44.2050      INR44.2350 \par  \par Forward Dollar Premiums/Discounts \par April                     July                     January \par INR0.2300 Vs INR0.2450    INR0.3750 Vs INR0.3850   INR0.630 Vs INR0.640 \par  \par Daily Overnight Reverse Repurchase Auction Amount \par Tuesday          Previous \par INR148.25 bln    INR179.20 bln \par  \par Reverse Repurchase Auction Rate \par Tuesday          Previous \par 5.50%           5.50% \par  \par Daily Overnight Repurchase Auction Amount \par Tuesday          Previous \par INR700 mln       INR1 bln \par  \par Repurchase Auction Rate \par Tuesday          Previous \par 6.50%           6.50% \par  \par Call Rate \par Tuesday          Previous \par 6.90%-7.10%     7.00%-7.25% \par  \par Interest Rate Swaps  Current Price   Previous Price \par  2-Year Mifor swap    6.11%-6.16%      6.19%-6.24% \par  5-Year Mifor swap    6.31%-6.36%      6.39%-6.44% \par  5-Year OIS           6.72%-6.73%      6.69%-6.70% \par  \par Benchmark Bond Prices \par Security   Maturity   Current Price   Previous Price \par  7.37% GOI   2014        100.80          101.10 \