\par\par \b \uc2 Dlr Off Early Highs Vs India Rupee On Portfolio Inflows  \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2006\par 10:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee rose against the dollar in intraday trading Tuesday as banks and other investors sold the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid continued inflows into the local stock market.  \par \par \uc2 At 0940 GMT, the dollar was at INR44.2000, off a high of INR44.3075 earlier in the day. It closed at INR44.2350 Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Foreigners have bought stocks worth $375 million so far this month, following purchases worth $805 million in January, that helped the Bombay Stock Exchange scale the 10,000 mark Monday.  \par \par \uc2 State-run banks that had been buying the greenback for the past two days, possibly on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , took a breather, adding to the rupee's gains. [ 07-02-06 0948GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over the last few sessions, buying the U.S. dollar to keep the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating too much.  \par \par \uc2 But they scaled back their purchases later in the session Tuesday, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "The rupee has been strengthening in line with the dollar's recent weakness overseas," said a trader at a European bank.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar fell to a new four-month low of INR44.07 against the rupee last week as foreign funds bought into Asia's fastest growing economy after China.  \par \par \uc2 "They have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curtail the rupee's overvaluation against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a trade-weighted basis," Sundeep Bhandari, regional head, global markets-South Asia, Standard Chartered Bank told Dow Jones Newswires.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained 1.87% against the U.S. unit since the start of 2006. Analysts say it is already 8%-9% overvalued in trade-weighted terms.  \par \par \uc2 -By Saikat Chatterjee; Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; djn.in@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Gauri Bhatia [ 07-02-06 1021GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060207e227000jc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
