\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee steady on foreign inflows, eyes cbank  \b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2006\par 03:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  (Updates to open)  \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, Feb 6 (Reuters) - The rupee shrugged off the dollar's strength overseas to trade steady on Monday, helped by foreign capital inflows but traders were wary that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could check more gains.  \par \par \uc2  At 9:40 a.m. (0410 GMT), the rupee <INR=IN> was quoted at 44.18/20 per dollar, little changed from Friday's close of 44.1950/2050 when it rose 0.13 percent.  \par \par \uc2  "The rupee is unlikely to break 44.20 as we could see dollar demand from importers or even state-run banks acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said the chief dealer at an Indian bank.  \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is on a firm footing so it is unlikely the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would allow the rupee to appreciate."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past few sessions, absorbing most of the foreign inflows.  \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which involves selling rupees to buy dollars, was probably to ease tight money in the banking system ahead of a 60-billion-rupee government bond sale on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2  In early Asian trade, the dollar was at 118.70 yen <JPY=>, in sight of a seven-week high after an upward revision in U.S. jobs data and a fall in the unemployment rate last week reinforced expectations for higher U.S. interest rates.  \par \par \uc2  Many in the market say that if the interest rate gap narrows between India and the United States it could hurt the rupee since the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is supported by foreign capital in search of extra yield.  \par \par \uc2  Traders were keeping an eye on crude oil prices, which surged after Iran resumed uranium enrichment and ended United Nations checks of its nuclear sites in response to being reported to the Security Council over concerns it is building nuclear weapons.  \par \par \uc2  Oil is India's biggest import and a surge in prices will widen India's trade deficit, putting pressure on the rupee.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ------------------------------------------------------------\par                                MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060209e2260006q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
