\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Higher,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears surface  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Vidya Ranganathan  \par \uc2 799 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2006\par 03:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Feb 1 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  bucked the dollar's strength against the yen on Wednesday and hit multi-year highs against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , raising concerns that regional central banks will step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 In late Asian trading, the Korean won <KRW=>, Singapore dollar <SGD=>, Thai baht <THB=> and Philippine peso <PHP=> were off their intra-day peaks against the dollar. Traders suspected central banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Korea had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The moves took place even as the U.S. dollar remained near a four-week high against the yen <JPY=> after the Federal Reserve raised interest rates as expected on Tuesday for the 14th time in a 19-month tightening cycle. The Fed also indicated further tightening could follow.  \par \par \uc2 The peso ended at 52.09 per dollar, just off a high of 52.05, its strongest level since May 2003 as markets positioned for foreign investment in Philippine equities.  \par \par \uc2 The won briefly hit 957 per dollar, last seen when Asia was in the midst of a financial crisis in November 1997, before retreating modestly.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht crept to the firmer side of 39 per dollar and then fell back, while the Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> stayed close to 9,300 per dollar and at its highest since March.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar met resistance near 1.6207 per U.S. dollar, some distance away from last week's highs around 1.6170.  \par \par \uc2 Markets in China, Malaysia and Taiwan remained closed for the Lunar New Year holidays.  \par \par \uc2 Mirza Baig, a Deutsche Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist, said operators who had been bearish were now buying Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 However, he said he would hesitate to buy Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at these levels.  \par \par \uc2 "The speculative position overhang has become extended and there is a higher probability of a squeeze like the one we saw in dollar/yen overnight.  \par \par \uc2 "People have realised that Asia is appreciating and have jumped on the bandwagon and we are likely to see a correction in the next few days."  \par \par \uc2 Manila-based traders said the peso was approaching resistance between 52 and 51.80, the latter level being the May 2003 peak.  \par \par \uc2 Expectations of foreign portfolio inflows underpinned sentiment. Foreigners have bought a net $2.35 billion of South Korean shares in the past 10 sessions.  \par \par \uc2 In the Philippines, news that 80 percent of power producer First Generation Corp.'s 8.5 billion peso IPO had been sold to overseas investors buoyed the peso.  \par \par \uc2 SING DOLLAR SEEN CAPPED  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the Sing dollar's 2.5 percent rise last month had pushed it to the top of what they estimated was the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy band for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that markets should be on guard for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) conducts monetary policy by managing the Singapore dollar within an undisclosed band against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Rising asset prices, robust export growth and the strength in economic growth numbers have prompted thinking among economists that the MAS is on the verge of announcing a policy suggesting a faster pace of appreciation for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 UBS's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Ashley Davies said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was about 1.8 percent stronger than his estimate of the mid-point of the band. UBS assumes the band is 4 percent wide and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows a modest pace of appreciation for this mid-point, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Davies said the Singapore dollar would now be stable, but could gain further in the medium term.  \par \par \uc2 "We still think that SGD will perform well on a medium-term view given the potential for the MAS to adopt a more aggressive tightening bias, should the strong data continue," he said in a note.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0931 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       117.67         117.35       -0.27\par  Sing dlr        1.6263         1.6233       -0.18\par  Korean won      962.00         964.60       +0.27\par  Baht             39.20          39.03       -0.43\par  Peso             52.03          52.17       +0.27\par  Rupiah         9310.00        9385.00       +0.81\par  Rupee            44.19          44.11       -0.18\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       117.67         117.96       +0.25\par  Sing dlr        1.6263         1.6625       +2.23\par  Korean won      962.00        1011.60       +5.16\par  Baht             39.20          41.11       +4.87\par  Peso             52.03          53.09       +2.04\par  Rupiah         9310.00        98