\par\par \b \uc2 Indian cbank stayed away from  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market in Nov  \b0\par\par\uc2 115 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2006\par 14:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Jan 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the third straight month in November after having bought a net $4 billion in the preceding three months.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India's monthly bulletin released on Thursday showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also kept away from the forward market, as in the earlier month.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a net $20.85 billion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market between April 2004 and March 2005 as it sought to rein in the rupee to maintain \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|SNS|SNI|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060119e21j00133\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
