\par\par \b \uc2 India Rupee Ends At 3-Mo High On Global Cues; Bonds Dn  \b0\par\par\uc2 908 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2006\par 14:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee ended at a fresh three-month high against the dollar Thursday, tracking the rise of other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. unit.  \par \par \uc2 Expectations that capital inflows will continue to remain robust also supported trade, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at INR44.1350, last tested Oct. 3 and nearly 0.4% below Tuesday's INR44.3100 close. Indian financial markets were closed Wednesday for a religious festival holiday.  \par \par \uc2 "Dollar/rupee was only following a global trend today, but with every sharp downward move, expectations the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  were rising," said a senior dealer at a foreign bank.  \par \par \uc2 Contrary to expectations, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday. The RBI was expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the country's export competitiveness and check volatility.  \par \par \uc2 "It took the rupee two months to fall from INR44.43 in October to INR46.33 in December but in just under a month, the rupee has risen by more than that," said an analyst at a private-sector bank. He noted the rupee was almost 8% overvalued in trade-weighted terms and a correction was due.  \par \par \uc2 "But as long as the rupee is tracking global trends, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be comfortable. RBI is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless dollar-rupee falls sharply below 44," he added.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to boost money market liquidity, which has shrunk in recent weeks.  \par \par \uc2 Surplus banking system liquidity has dwindled in recent weeks, triggered by the redemption of the State Bank of India's (500112.BY) $7.3 billion India Millennium Deposits - the country's largest-ever capital outflow - in December after companies paid nearly INR200 billion in quarterly taxes.  \par \par \uc2 Strong demand for bank loans has also put pressure on system liquidity. Latest data show bank loans grew 30% in the year to Dec. 23, well above 19% growth in deposits during the same period.  \par \par \uc2 Crunched system cash hit the market for interbank funds, pushing up the call money rate to over 7.0% from a notional 5.25% floor in recent sessions, making bond investments more expensive. The rate ended steady at 7.00%-7.25% Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "Strong credit growth, a large capital outflow in December and recent bond auctions (INR100 billion Monday) have squeezed money market liquidity," said a local dealer. "Cash will remain tight until government spending picks up."  \par \par \uc2 The RBI infused about INR282 billion at the day's repurchase auction, up from INR245 previously, reflecting shrinking system funds.  \par \par \uc2 Although liquidity is expected to improve once the government resumes spending on infrastructure and salaries this month, the federal government's next bond auction, worth INR140 billion, in February, is expected to again dent system cash.  \par \par \uc2 Indian government bonds ended down as investors sold bonds amid thin volumes in directionless trade. Most participants stayed on the sidelines, hoping for cues on yield direction when the RBI meets to review policy Jan. 24.  \par \par \uc2 "Cash should improve next week, there are some inflows from treasury bill redemptions (around INR38 billion) due tomorrow," said a local dealer. "Also, banks ease off product covering in the second week of the reporting fortnight, so call rates are likely to come off."  \par \par \uc2 Banks typically borrow funds in the call money market to cover reserve needs and report average cash reserve positions to the RBI every two weeks. The current reporting cycle ends next Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The popular 7.27% 2013 bond ended lower at INR102.08 from INR102.09 previously. Its yield closed unchanged at 6.91%.  \par \par \uc2 In the forward segment, dollar rates ended higher as tightening system liquidity pressured money market interest rates up. The dollar forward contract maturing in December 2006 closed at a premium of INR0.6200, from INR0.5800 previously.  \par \par \uc2 Interest rate swaps benchmarked to the Mumbai interbank forward offered rate, or MIFOR, rose on large overseas corporate hedging to the tune of nearly $500 million-$1 billion. The five-year swap ended higher at 6.36%-6.41% from 6.35%-6.39.  \par \par \uc2 Overnight indexed swap rates ended up on worries about tight liquidity. The five-year swap ended up at 6.41%-6.43% from 6.38%-6.39%. [ 12-01-06 1318GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Rupee Vs Dollar Close \par Thursday        Previous \par INR44.1350      INR44.3100 \par  \par Forward Dollar Premiums/Discounts \par March                    June                     December \par INR0.2700 Vs INR0.2450   INR0.4200 Vs INR0.3800   INR0.6200 Vs INR0.5800 \par  \par Daily Overnight Reverse Repurchase Auction Amount \par Thursday         Previous \par INR8.45 bln      INR6.25 bln \par  \par Reverse Repurchase Auction Rate \par Thursday         Previous \par 5.25%            5.25% \par  \par Daily Overnight Repurchase Auction Amount \par Thursday         Previous \par INR282.15 bln    INR245.20 bln \par  \par Repurchase Auction Rate \par Thursday         Previous \par 6.25%            6.25% \par  \par Call Rate \par Thursday         Previous \par 7.00%-7.25%      7.00%-7.25% \par  \par Interest Rate Swaps  Curre