\par\par \b \uc2 RBI WATCH: India Unlikely To Stem Rupee Slide For Now  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Anil Varma  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 1,047 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2005\par 04:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Reserve Bank of India has finally signaled what many \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants had suspected - that the rupee's recent weakness isn't yet a concern for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  so it won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deteriorating current account deficit and relatively expensive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trade-weighted terms mean that the RBI appears happy to let rupee weaken against the dollar, which has strengthened against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say that the rupee's weakness won't start to worry the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade-weighted overvaluation is significantly reduced.  \par \par \uc2 Some in the market expect the RBI to step in if the dollar breaks strong resistance at INR46.50, which is a level that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tested but failed to break more than 15 months ago. Market watchers say this level could break in coming weeks.  \par \par \uc2 RBI Deputy Governor Rakesh Mohan said late Wednesday that the rupee market has been "very orderly" of late, and that "genuine" dollar demand caused a sharp recent rupee fall.  \par \par \uc2 "Yes, of course, the rupee has been moving but...it has been moving in two directions - it is what a healthy market ought to have," Mohan told reporters when asked about the rupee's sharpest six-week fall in over a year.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar has risen 4.5% against the rupee so far this fiscal year, which started on April 1. It gained 3.9% in the past six weeks alone. The last time the dollar rose as much against the rupee over as short a period was in April and May 2004. The dollar closed at INR45.81 Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't have a target level or range for the rupee, but often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to smooth market volatility. But the RBI so far has done little to slow the rupee's accelerated fall in recent weeks.  \par \par \uc2 The government too has indicated it isn't concerned about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister P. Chidambaram said Wednesday that "orderly movement" of the rupee is acceptable as long as such moves are in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade-weighted value.  \par \par \uc2 Most analysts expect the rupee to extend losses in the coming weeks although some anticipate a partial recovery later, helped by a recovery in inflows of foreign investment into the local stock market.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar can still head higher against the rupee in the short term, possibly testing the INR47 level. But I expect it to stabilize around the INR46 level by year-end helped by an improvement in foreign equity flows," said JPMorgan Chase Bank's Asian head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy, Claudio Piron. Foreigners bought local shares worth $353.4 million so far this month, after making sales worth $866 million last month.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      Current Account Has Deteriorated \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite its recent fall, the rupee remains significantly overvalued in trade-weighted terms, indicating there is room for further weakness.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts estimate that an index of the rupee's real effective exchange rate, or its value in trade-weighted terms, is currently above 107, indicating overvaluation of more than 7%. The rupee is considered at fair value when its REER is 100.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The market will take dollar-rupee to a level that is justified by fundamentals such as the trade-weighted valuation of the rupee...that shouldn't be a cause for concern for the RBI," said Agam Gupta, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading at Standard Chartered Bank India.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  watchers say the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is tolerating rupee weakness because it reflects the dollar's global strengthening and India's current account deficit.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The RBI's comments confirm that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  isn't uneasy about the rupee's weakness...(and) that the RBI believes the rupee fall reflects fundamentals such as the current account deficit and the dollar's global strengthening," said P.H. Ramaswamy, managing director at Calyon India.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's current account swung to a $6.20 billion deficit in the April-June quarter from a $3.39 billion surplus in the same quarter a year earlier.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economists expect the deficit for the whole of fiscal 2005-2006 in the $16 billion-$18 billion range, as high global oil prices inflate the country's oil import bill.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some say that the RBI also isn't likely concerned that a sharp rupee fall could damp import demand, which is a key driver of investment activity, because imports may be like exports and be unresponsive to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  changes.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "India's exports grew strongly when the rupee was strengthening so there isn't much reason to believe imports could contract due to a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fall," said Calyon's Ramaswamy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's exports rose 20.5% in the six months between April and September, compared with a year earlier, well above the government's 16% growth target for fiscal 2005-2006. Imports grew even faster at 33.1% during the same period.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the past, the RBI has mostly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market when it sensed speculation was making the market volatile.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But "at current levels of dollar-rupee, there is hardly any speculative activity," notes Pankaj Sharma, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealer at state-owned Union Bank of India.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sharma said the rupee's weakness reflected a dollar demand-supply gap of around $3 billion per month in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, caused by the current account shortfall and a slowdown in capital inflows due to rising U.S. interest rates.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A series of interest-rate hikes by the U.S. Federal Reserve since mid-2004 has sharply cut the U.S.-India interest-rate differential. The Fed has raised the Federal Funds rate by three percentage points to 4.00% since June 2004 while the RBI increased its benchmark rate by just 0.75 percentage point to 5.25%, narrowing the interest-rate gap by 2.25 percentage points to 1.25 percentage points.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Anil Varma, Dow Jones Newswires, 91 22 22884212; anil.varma\u174\'00\'AEdowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Anil Varma covers India's money and fixed income markets for Dow Jones Newswires.)  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -Edited by Iain McDonald \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 10-11-05 0339GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1078  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051110e1ba0007i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
