\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee eases to 44 per dlr, eyes cbank  \b0\par\par\uc2 193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2005\par 05:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Aug 30 (Reuters) - The rupee extended losses from the previous session's 8-1/2-month low, easing to 44 per dollar on Tuesday for the first time since Jan. 10, on concerns India's trade deficit will widen due to high oil prices.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said expectations of foreign fund outflows as the stock market slips also put downward pressure on the rupee, which lost 0.44 percent on Monday. A shortage of cash dollars and the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength overseas also combined to weigh on the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But traders expect \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupee. The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb excessive volatily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 At 9.05 a.m. (0335 GMT) the rupee <INR=IN> was quoted at 43.98/44.00 per dollar, weaker than the previous close of 43.8850/8900. It last closed weaker than this level on Jan. 10, when it finished at 43.94/96 against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (URGENT)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050830e18u0005x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
