\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee rises on weak dlr, but wary of oil  \b0\par\par\uc2 480 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2005\par 15:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 BOMBAY, Aug 12 (Reuters) - The rupee recovered from the previous day's one-month low to end firm on Friday as the dollar fell against major overseas \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But the gains were limited by a cash dollar shortage caused by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , record high oil prices fuelling concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ballooning trade deficit and commercial demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Rupee trading had finished before the release of U.S. data on the June trade deficit, which widened 6.1 percent to $58.82 billion from a revised $55.43 billion in May. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped further after the data.  \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible Indian rupee <INR=IN> ended at 43.5350/54 per dollar, 0.13 percent stronger than the previous close of 43.5925/5975, the lowest finish since July 8.  \par \par \uc2 "There was commercial and oil-related dollar demand, due to which some traders went long on the dollar. But with the extended weekend and the fall in dollar against majors, there was (dollar) selling later," said a chief dealer at an Indian bank.  \par \par \uc2 Banks in India's financial capital, Bombay, are shut on Monday due to a national holiday.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. light crude <CLc1> was up 25 cents at $66.05 a barrel on Friday, after charging to a record high of $66.15 as investors fret over the world's strained capacity to refine and pump crude.  \par \par \uc2 But traders said the rupee, which analysts say is overvalued by 9 percent on a trade-weighted basis, was supported by robust foreign fund flows into the booming stock market.  \par \par \uc2 The local unit has held its ground this year, helped by the $7.2 billion that foreign funds have moved into the Indian stock market since Jan. 1, which has helped lift the benchmark BSE index <.BSESN> by more than 18 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers are holding their annual meeting this weekend, and dealers will be looking for signals on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance on the rupee after China's revaluation last month and as foreign investors keep pumping in money.  \par \par \uc2 Almost 400 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers will meet in the southern city of Cochin from Aug. 13 to Aug. 15, where Shyamla Gopinath, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deputy governor in charge of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , will be the star speaker.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India, which stayed away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market between April and June, resumed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month after China's decision to revalue the yuan briefly lifted the rupee to a six-year peak to 43.12.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par                       MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index                 <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)                      <INR=IN>\par  7.38 percent 2015 bond (%)            <IN10YT=RR>\par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050812e18c001b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
