\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee slips on cash dollar shortage  \b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 2005\par 04:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 BOMBAY, Aug 8 (Reuters) - The rupee slid on Monday, dragged down by a cash dollar shortage that traders said had been triggered by the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sustained mop-up of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent sessions.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) resumed its rupee-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month, after a three-month gap, to pull the rupee back from a six-year peak of 43.115/135 struck in the wake of China's revaluation of the yuan.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by $3.06 billion in the week to July 29 to $140.6 billion as the RBI absorbed a bulk of the foreign capital flowing into local stocks.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee <INR=IN> closed at 43.5475/5525 per dollar, 0.15 percent weaker than its previous close of 43.4825/4850.  \par \par \uc2 "The cash dollar shortage and the sharp fall in local stocks weighed on the rupee," said a dealer at a foreign bank.  \par \par \uc2 Spot dollars usually trade at a premium to cash dollars, but they were quoted at a discount on Monday, meaning there was a shortage of cash dollars relative to demand.  \par \par \uc2 The Bombay stock index <.BSESN> ended 1.91 percent lower at 7,606.17 points on Monday after running up more than a quarter since early May as investors worried about high share valuations and the threat of higher oil prices to corporate earnings.  \par \par \uc2 Surging foreign fund investment of nearly $7 billion in India's booming stock market since the start of 2005 has been putting upward pressure on the rupee, which some analysts say is overvalued by about 9 percent. To see a related story, please double-click on [ID:nT41066].  \par \par \uc2 In European trade, the yen was at 111.62 yen per dollar <JPY=>, up 0.2 percent on the day, after hitting a week low of 112.62 yen. The dollar was down slightly against the euro at $1.2379 <EUR=>, but up from a two-month low around $1.24 hit last week.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. Labor Department said on Friday a total of 207,000 new non-farm payroll jobs were created in July, beating economists' median forecast of 183,000 and reinforcing expectations that the Fed will stick to its measured tightening.  \par \par \uc2 The Federal Open Market Committee is widely expected to raise its Fed funds rate by 25 basis points to 3.5 percent at its meeting on Tuesday, making it the tenth straight rate increase.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par                       MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index                 <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)                      <INR=IN>\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|RBN|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050808e1880013u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
