\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee edges up, cautious ahead of U.S. data  \b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2005\par 04:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 BOMBAY, Aug 5 (Reuters) - The rupee inched up on Friday on foreign capital inflows and dollar sales by exporters eyeing the euro's recent gains against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But caution ahead of key U.S. jobs data and wariness of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI), which has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  strongly in recent sessions, limited the rupee's gains, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee <INR=IN> closed at 43.4825/4850 per dollar, 0.1 percent stronger than Thursday's 43.5250/5275 close. It was unchanged on the week, held steady by a watchful RBI.  \par \par \uc2 "A weaker stock market, fear of Big Brother watching, U.S. data, weekend position squaring, all added to reduced speculative position build-up," a chief dealer at a foreign bank said.  \par \par \uc2 The Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which let the rupee gain 0.5 percent between April and June by staying on the sidelines, resumed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month after China's revaluation of the yuan by 2.1 percent lifted the rupee to a six-year peak of 43.115/135.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market volumes also dipped a little, with spot deals totalling $2.2 billion on Friday, down from $2.7 billion the previous day, according to data posted on The Clearing Corporation of India Ltd. website,  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.ccilindia.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.ccilindia.com }}}\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 In European trade, the dollar drifted in a tight range, having bounced off two-month lows against the euro <EUR=>, as investors shied away from making big bets ahead of the U.S. jobs data.  \par \par \uc2 Markets were waiting to see if the dollar could rally on the back of any surprise uptick in the July non-farm payrolls report.  \par \par \uc2 The jobs data due at 1230 GMT could set the pace of U.S. rate rises and impact yield differentials between the United States and Europe. Economists forecast 183,000 jobs were created in July.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee has been supported by foreign fund investment of $6.9 billion in India's booming stock market in 2005.  \par \par \uc2 India's benchmark Bombay stock index <.BSESN> snapped a nine-session rally on Friday, easing from a record high, tracking a pull-back in global equity markets.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par                       MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index                 <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)                      <INR=IN>\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|RBN|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050805e185001cp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
