\par\par \b \uc2 India Fin Min: Stk Mkt Reflects Current Econ Potential  \b0\par\par\uc2 426 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2005\par 13:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--India's Finance Minister P. Chidambaram said Friday the stock market trend showed the current economic potential of the country, but cautioned investors against excessive exuberance.  \par \par \uc2 Indian shares ended at a record high Friday on fund buying in blue chip shares amid hopes that the Chinese yuan revaluation would boost foreign fund inflows and lead to strong export growth for domestic companies.  \par \par \uc2 The Bombay Stock Exchange's 30-share Sensitive Index, or Sensex, rose sharply by 118.93 points, or 1.6%, to close at an all-time high of 7423.25.  \par \par \uc2 "Markets will rise and markets will fall...We urge investors that their response be measured," Chidambaram said at a tax conference.  \par \par \uc2 Chidambaram also said the Indian economy has the capacity to perform better than at present.  \par \par \uc2 India's economy is expected to grow 7% during the current fiscal year that started April, from 6.9% in the previous year. [ 22-07-05 1135GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Turning to China's revaluation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Chidambaram said the development is unlikely to have a "major impact" on India.  \par \par \uc2 "As far as the government is concerned, and as far as the RBI is concerned, this won't change our exchange rate policy," he said.  \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, China scrapped the yuan's peg to the dollar and said it would now use a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to manage the yuan.  \par \par \uc2 As part of the move, the People's Bank of China revalued the yuan to CNY8.11 to the U.S. dollar, effectively a 2% increase in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value.  \par \par \uc2 Soon after China's move, the rupee strengthened, hitting a six-year high Friday against the U.S. dollar, which touched INR43.14.  \par \par \uc2 Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  later in the day pulled the dollar up. At 1140 GMT the dollar was at INR43.47, up from its close of INR43.22 Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Asked about prospects for local interest rates, Chidambaram didn't reply directly, but said: "There is enough liquidity in the market today."  \par \par \uc2 The market has been expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise the reverse repurchase rate by 25 basis points from the current 5% since RBI Governor Y.V. Reddy last week said global uncertainties had gone beyond the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's estimate.  \par \par \uc2 The RBI is scheduled to detail its quarterly review of monetary policy Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Anil Varma, Dow Jones Newswires; +91-11-2307 4020; venkat.pr@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited By Paul Baylis [ 22-07-05 1151GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050722e17m000j0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
