\par\par \b \uc2 Indian cbank panel wants  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  controls relaxed  \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2005\par 15:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BOMBAY, June 24 (Reuters) - An Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  panel on Friday recommended the country, which is sitting on a huge pile of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, should further relax capital controls and push forward more reforms in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 To allow more hedging flexibility, the panel said residents should be allowed to cancel and rebook foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, while companies should deal in covered call and put options.  \par \par \uc2 And Indian banks should be allowed to accept deposits from non-resident Indians in more foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Canadian dollar, Australian dollar and New Zealand dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The panel's report has been posted on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's website:  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.rbi.org.in"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.rbi.org.in }}}\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 India's rupee is only partially convertible and last month, in a bid to curb speculation and develop a local long-term forward rupee-dollar curve, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  barred a foreign benchmark to price a key interest rate derivative used by companies to hedge foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposures.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings, which has boosted \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to $138 billion from about $25 billion five years back.  \par \par \uc2 Since the reserves could pay for 15 months of imports, analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should relax its strict capital controls, imposed decades ago when foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was scarce.  \par \par \uc2 The committee has also recommended that certain banks, trading in India's $9 billion-a-day \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, should be allowed to hedge commodity risks for corporate clients and provide capital against their actual open exchange position.  \par \par \uc2 "Banks may be given the freedom to decide on the period of crystallisation of unpaid export bills," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.  \par \par \uc2 The committee also said \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  data including traded volumes for derivatives, such as foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rupee options, should be made available to the market on a regular basis.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|SNS|SNI|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050624e16o0013t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
