\par\par \b \uc2 India may allow rupee to rise on inflation, yuan  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Anirban Nag  \par \uc2 726 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2005\par 09:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BOMBAY, May 12 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may allow the rupee to gain gradually in the next few weeks in a bid to stave off rising inflation and as it prepares the ground for a possible revaluation of the Chinese yuan, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> surged to a 5-\u189\'00\'BD year peak of 43.26 per dollar on Wednesday after a Chinese newspaper report -- that was denied by China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- suggested Beijing would revalue the tightly controlled yuan as early as next week.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee has since retreated to 43.29 but analysts say a stronger yuan would boost other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and speculation a move is close has been one factor behind recent rupee gains.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise after it hit a five-year high in February but, with interest rates rising and wholesale price inflation pushing up to 6 percent from around 5 percent in March, keeping it down could prove tough.  \par \par \uc2 "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) will have no choice but to let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate in the medium term," said Bhanu Baweja, strategist at UBS in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 "It's the unholy trinity -- interest rates, inflation and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- and one cannot control all of them together. I expect the rupee to touch 42.50 by December-end as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seeks to manage inflation."  \par \par \uc2 The RBI says it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to smooth volatility rather than target an exchange rate level but it successfully drove the rupee back from February's high with large-scale selling.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted its short-term interest rate by 25 basis points to 5.0 percent on April 28, citing inflation concerns in Asia's fourth-largest economy.  \par \par \uc2 In its statement it saw firm crude oil prices as a permanent feature, igniting talk the rupee may be allowed to rise to help offset imported inflation.  \par \par \uc2 India imports 70 percent of its crude oil and while the government has frozen local fuel prices since November it is debating whether to raise them so they align more with higher global prices. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  estimates every $1 rise in crude oil adds 30 basis points to the wholesale price index.  \par \par \uc2 CHINESE REVALUATION  \par \par \uc2 The rupee's rise and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's absence from the market in recent weeks have coincided with market expectations China's yuan could be revalued soon.  \par \par \uc2 "The talk of a yuan revaluation is coming at a time when I think the RBI may allow a gradual appreciation in the rupee to check inflation," said M.G. Srinivas, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at ING Vysya Bank, Bangalore. He expected the rupee to touch 43.10 by mid-June.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Yaga Venugopal Reddy said two weeks ago he did not expect an adverse impact on the rupee from a potential revaluation of the yuan. But he said the authority was watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market carefully.  \par \par \uc2 Rajeev Malik, senior economist at JP Morgan in Singapore, said the rupee could gain to 43.0, although it may correct a little now the immediate revaluation speculation had faded.  \par \par \uc2 He said the rupee was overvalued on a real effective exchange rate but the RBI would consider how far other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would rise against the dollar if the yuan was revalued.  \par \par \uc2 "That gives them some flexibility not to do anything. Technically, it would be a structural change."  \par \par \uc2 Trade between India and China quadrupled between 2000 and 2004 to $13 billion and Reddy said recently India was likely to benefit in trade terms if the yuan was revalued, a comment which boosted the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 Trade with Japan was worth just $4.4 billion in 2004 but Japan is one of five economies -- including the United States, Britain, France and Germany -- in a trade-weighted basket which analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  watches to monitor the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 "As China's importance as a trading partner grows with India, the renminbi will eventually be included in the five-country basket," said Prasenjit Basu, managing director Robust Economic Analysis in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 "So the renminbi will have a modest influence on the rupee's movement."  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-INDIA-RUPEE|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050512e15c000r0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
