\par\par \b \uc2 India Rupee Rally On Bogus Yuan Reform Report; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 799 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2005\par 14:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee rallied to its highest level since July 1999 against the dollar Wednesday after a bogus report on the Web site of one of China's top official newspapers said Beijing was about to announce a revaluation of the yuan.  \par \par \uc2 But the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended slightly below its intraday high after China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  subsequently said it had no new information on the yuan exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at a 70-month low of INR43.2850 Wednesday, down from INR43.4350 at the previous close, but above the day's low of INR43.2600.  \par \par \uc2 A report on the English-language Web site of the People's Daily, the official mouthpiece of the Chinese Communist Party, said an expansion of the yuan's narrow trading band against the dollar "will be announced" at an unspecified time. It said the resulting rise of the yuan was estimated at 1.26% within a month and 6.03% within a year after a meeting between Chinese and U.S. financial officials.  \par \par \uc2 The story, which sent the dollar down against most Asian units, was later removed from the Web site.  \par \par \uc2 "China is one of India's competitors in the global exports market. If the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is allowed to strengthen, that would definitely give the rupee more room to rise," said a trader at a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained 4.3% against the dollar in the past six months, mainly due to capital inflows into the local stock market and the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's global weakness.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee is currently overvalued by nearly 6% in trade-weighted terms and the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in recent months to check its gains and protect export competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 However, many \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -watchers now believe the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would loosen its grip on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if China allowed the yuan to strengthen. The prospects of higher inflation may also spur the RBI to tolerate a more gradual appreciation of the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 Dollar forward rates ended lower Wednesday, tracking the trend in the spot market. The forward contract maturing in April 2006 closed at a premium of INR0.545 to the spot rate, down from INR0.585 at Tuesday's close.  \par \par \uc2 MIFOR-based interest rate swaps closed lower. The five-year swap ended at 5.93%-5.98%, while the two-year swap was at 5.41%-5.45%.  \par \par \uc2 Overnight index swaps ended steady, with the five-year swap closing at 6.59%-6.61%.  \par \par \uc2 Indian government bond prices ended marginally higher Wednesday on mild bargain hunting by traders after prices fell in early trade following an RBI announcement of a state government bond auction.  \par \par \uc2 The widely traded 7.55% paper, due 2010, ended at INR102.92, up from INR102.85 at Tuesday's close. Its yield slipped to 6.85% from 6.87%.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier, bond prices slipped after the RBI announced a state government bond sale late Tuesday evening after the market closed for trading.  \par \par \uc2 Twenty-six of India's 29 state governments plan to sell 7.77% 10-year bonds worth INR73 billion Tuesday. The Reserve Bank of India said in a press release the bond sale will be on-tap. Under the on-tap method, bonds are sold at a fixed price until stocks last.  \par \par \uc2 "Bonds may remain in tight range Thursday as there are no triggers available till the bond auction next week," said a dealer at a state-run bank. "Most market participants are also waiting for the U.S. trade data release later today," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight call money rate ended mostly steady Wednesday at 4.95%-5.05%, compared with 4.90%-5.05% at the previous close in plentiful money market liquidity. [ 11-05-05 1259GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Rupee Vs Dollar Close \par Wednesday       Previous \par INR43.2850      INR43.4350 \par  \par Forward Dollar Premiums/Discounts \par July                   October                April \par INR0.1600 Vs INR0.1625 INR0.3200 Vs INR0.3325 INR0.545 Vs INR0.585 \par  \par Daily Overnight Reverse Repurchase Auction Amount \par Wednesday       Previous \par INR174.10 Bln   INR200.70 Bln \par  \par Reverse Repurchase Auction Rate \par Wednesday       Previous \par 5.00%           5.00% \par  \par Call Rate \par Wednesday       Previous Close \par 4.95%-5.05%     4.90%-5.05% \par  \par Interest Rate Swaps  Current Price   Previous Price \par  2-Year Mifor swap   5.41%-5.45%     5.45%-5.50% \par  5-Year Mifor swap   5.93%-5.98%     6.00%-6.05% \par  5-Year OIS          6.59%-6.61%     6.59%-6.61% \par  \par Benchmark Bond Prices \par Security   Maturity   Current Price   Previous Price \par  7.55% GOI   2010        102.92          102.85 \par  7.38% GOI   2015        101.30          101.27 \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Madhu T, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; madhu.nair@dowjones.com [ 11-05-05 1259GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050511e15b000tp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
