\par\par \b \uc2 Dlr Falls Vs India Rupee To INR43.2600 Vs INR43.4350 Tue  \b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2005\par 10:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee climbed to its highest level since July 1999 against the U.S. dollar Wednesday after reported comments by a Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official sparked increased speculation that China may soon re-value its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar temporarily fell to INR43.2600 in Wednesday's afternoon trading from INR43.4350 at the previous close, before partly retracing its fall on interbank bargain hunting. At 0900 GMT, the dollar was at INR43.2800. [ 11-05-05 0911GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 People's Bank of China Deputy Governor Wu Xiaoling was reported to have said in an interview with the major Japanese financial daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun that the bank is now "technically" prepared to carry out \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reforms.  \par \par \uc2 "China is one of India's competitors in the global exports market. If the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is allowed to strengthen, that would definitely give the rupee more room to rise," said a trader at a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the rupee's advance against the dollar Wednesday reflected similar gains by most other Asian units.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained 4.3% against the dollar in the past six months mainly due to capital inflows into the local stock market and the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's global weakness.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee is currently overvalued by nearly 6% in trade-weighted terms and the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in recent months to check its gains and protect export competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 However, many \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers now believe the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would loosen its grip on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if China allows the yuan to strengthen. The prospects of higher inflation may also spur the RBI to tolerate a more gradual appreciation of the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 -By Anil Varma, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; anil.varma@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -Edited by Paul Baylis \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 11-05-05 0956GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050511e15b000gn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
