\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee seen rangebound, U.S. data awaited.  \b0\par\par\uc2 249 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2005\par 04:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, April 12 (Reuters) - The rupee is seen rangebound\par on Tuesday, after climbing to three-week highs the previous\par day, as dealers watch the dollar's moves overseas and await\par U.S. trade data.\par     The dollar drifted to a one-week low against the yen in\par Asian trade, while the euro was little changed after rising on\par Monday.\par  \par     "U.S. data could give direction to the market," said a\par dealer at a foreign bank.\par     Although U.S. trade figures are forecast to show the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 second-biggest deficit ever, traders in Japan said the data was  \f28 \par \par \uc2 unlikely to depress the market for long and that the dollar  \par \par \uc2 would stay supported on expectations for higher U.S. interest  \par \par \uc2 rates.  \par \par \uc2 Traders will scrutinise minutes of the Federal Reserve's  \par \par \uc2 March policy meeting for clues on U.S. interest rates. Signs  \par \par \uc2 that rates may rise faster have helped the dollar and raised  \par \par \uc2 concerns that investment in developing countries may wane.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee climbed to 43.7110/7150 a dollar on  \par \par \uc2 Monday, its strongest since March 18 and up 0.13 percent on the  \par \par \uc2 day as the dollar weakened against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dealers also took some comfort from a lull in \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 action to curb rupee gains. The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively through much of February to limit rupee  \par \par \uc2 strength after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  set five-year highs early in the  \par \par \uc2 month.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par     Bombay Sensitive Index\par     Indian rupee (/$)\par     7.38 percent 2015 bond (%)\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050412e14c003eb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
