\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee ends lower as dlr firm, inflows prop.  \b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 13:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, March 28 (Reuters) - The rupee ended weaker on\par Monday, as dollar's gains overseas prompted some demand for the\par U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  among importers but robust capital inflows,\par accumulated over the Easter weekend, helped limit losses.\par     The rupee          closed at 43.7850/7900 per dollar, 0.08\par percent weaker than its previous close of 43.7500/7550. It was,\par however, off a 43.8200 session low.\par     "The dollar's gains overseas both against the euro and the\par yen clearly pushed up demand for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," a trading head\par at a private bank said.\par  \par     "But the bunched up weekend inflows and some fund buying in\par the stock market, which gained 1 percent today, helped."\par     The dollar was holding firm at a four-and-a-half month high\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against the yen and near a six-week peak versus the euro on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 expectations that upcoming U.S. jobs data would give the  \par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve another reason to raise interest rates more  \par \par \uc2 aggressively.  \par \par \uc2 With European markets closed on Monday for the Easter  \par \par \uc2 holidays, the dollar was at 106.77/82 yen and the euro  \par \par \uc2 was at $1.2923/29 in late Asian trade.  \par \par \uc2 The Federal Reserve raised rates last week by a quarter  \par \par \uc2 percentage point as expected and said a faster pace of future  \par \par \uc2 U.S. rate rises was possible to ward off inflation.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the rupee was likely to stay under pressure on  \par \par \uc2 Tuesday ahead of the month end and as India's April-March  \par \par \uc2 fiscal year draws to a close, triggering some dollar demand  \par \par \uc2 from companies seeking to make routine import-related and  \par \par \uc2 interest payments.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee has been kept on a tight leash by sustained  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since scaling a five-year peak of  \par \par \uc2 43.30 in early February and has now lost nearly three-quarters  \par \par \uc2 of a percent in 2005, despite robust foreign fund inflows.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 to keep the rupee's appreciation from hurting export  \par \par \uc2 competitiveness, as it tries to contain a widening trade  \par \par \uc2 deficit.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par     Bombay Sensitive Index\par     Indian rupee (/$)\par     7.38 percent 2015 bond (%)\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050328e13s009na\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
