\par\par \b \uc2 India Markets-Stocks and bonds tumble on record oil prices.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Atiya Hussain  \par \uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 14:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BOMBAY, March 17 (Reuters) - Bombay shares tumbled more than 1 percent and government bonds slid to nearly six-week lows as U.S. crude oil prices surged to record highs above $57 a barrel, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again sent the rupee lower on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee weakened for the third straight day as the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) stepped up its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on worries high oil prices would worsen \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade deficit, on course for a record in the current financial year ending on March 31.  \par \par \uc2 The Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended at 43.6550/6650 per dollar, retreating further from a five-week closing high of 43.55/56 set on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 30-share Bombay index closed 1.15 percent lower at 6,669.52 points, its lowest close since March 1, weighed down by record high oil prices that fuelled fears of rising inflation in the energy-hungry country.  \par \par \uc2 In spite of the losses, shares of UTV Software Communications Ltd. jumped on the debut of the television show producer. UTV rose as much as 35 percent to 175.40 rupees before closing at 168.50 rupees.  \par \par \uc2 Signs that foreign buying, a key support to shares and the rupee, has slowed also weighed on the share index, dealers said. Data on Wednesday showed that foreign funds were net sellers of local shares on Tuesday for the first time since Jan. 25.  \par \par \uc2 The Bombay index climbed to record highs above 6,900 last week, rallying on strong foreign investment inflows. Foreign funds have bought some $4 billion worth of Indian shares so far in 2005 - nearly half of last year's record level.  \par \par \uc2 "The figures for foreign fund inflows were negative yesterday. That was a little unnerving. High oil prices are acting as a bit of a dampener as well," said Raju Mewawalla, a relationship manager at Emkay Share and Stock Brokers.  \par \par \uc2 India imports 70 percent of its crude oil needs and an oil spike drove the domestic inflation rate to a 3-1/2-year high of 8.74 percent last August, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise interest rates for the first time in four years in October.  \par \par \uc2 The yield on the 10-year benchmark bond ended at 6.6740 percent on Thursday, its highest since Feb. 5, as dealers eyed surging world oil prices and awaited a slew of federal debt issuances in the new year starting in April.  \par \par \uc2 The Indian economy is poised to grow nearly 7 percent in the current fiscal year but a continued rise in oil prices could pose a problem next year. Analysts said a $5 per barrel rise in oil prices would cost 0.5 percentage points of economic growth. ((Reporting by Arif Sharif, Anirban Nag, editing by Sugita Katyal; Reuters Messaging: atiya.hussain.reuters.com@reuters.net; +91 22 5636 9263)).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050317e13h00avs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
