\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2  reserves at record high on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Anirban Nag  \par \uc2 547 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 09:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BOMBAY, March 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose by nearly $2 billion to a record high in the week to March 4 as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  worked to keep exports competitive by absorbing equity investments from foreigners, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 Data from the Reserve Bank of India on Saturday showed the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to $137.56 billion on March 4 from $135.66 billion a week earlier, the fourth consecutive weekly increase.  \par \par \uc2 India's reserves holdings are the sixth largest in the world.  \par \par \uc2 "Clearly we are seeing increased presence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and this is driving up reserves," said Shubhada Rao, director at Economic Consulting Group, Bombay.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar's weakness in past week against the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should also boost reserves in the near term."  \par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, Yaga Venugopal Reddy, said last month that large foreign inflows posed a challenge to exchange rate management and monetary policy.  \par \par \uc2 Overseas portfolio investors have pumped nearly $3.3 billion into stocks this year, more than a third of 2004's record $8.5 billion, on expectations of increased corporate profits.  \par \par \uc2 The inflows have driven India's key stock index to a record high, hit on March 9, putting pressure on the rupee to strengthen and prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee hit a five-year high of 43.30 per dollar in early February, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar buying since then has driven it down 0.6 percent to 43.57 on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seeks to keep the Indian rupee in a 3 to 5 percent trading band, and has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in a bid to ensure that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not highly overvalued on a trade-weighted basis.  \par \par \uc2 DIVERSIFICATION  \par \par \uc2 On Friday, Reddy told reporters that diversification of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves was being discussed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , similar to recent comments from Japan and South Korea, the world's first and fourth largest holders of reserves.  \par \par \uc2 "Yes it is being discussed. We are always discussing. It's a continuous process," Reddy said. "It is an ongoing debate with all central banks and you cannot expect a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor to say anything further on this."  \par \par \uc2 His comments sparked speculation on whether the talk of diversification was part of a coordinated plan by Asian central banks.  \par \par \uc2 Asian economies hold almost $2.5 trillion of reserves, and the majority are thought to be invested in U.S. dollar assets. Talk of a shift away from dollars, either in existing holdings or in allocations of new reserves, creates a great deal of nervousness in global markets over the dollar's prospects.  \par \par \uc2 Asia's sharp build-up in reserves in recent years - India's have almost doubled since the end of 2002 - has limited falls in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar and helped keep the region's exports competitive.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar has been under pressure because of the huge U.S. budget and current account deficits. It hit a record low against the euro at the end of 2004, and has hit multi-year lows against a number of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050312e13c004mq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
