\par\par \b \uc2 India cbank lets rupee edge up, ends at 1-mth high.  \b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 12:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, March 11 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee posted its\par best close in a month for a second day on Friday as a watchful\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  loosened its grip slightly towards the close,\par letting the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ride up a little on strong capital\par inflows.\par     The rupee          ended at 43.5600/5650 per dollar, a gain\par of 0.07 percent from Thursday's 43.5850/5950 close and the best\par finish since 43.50/51 on Feb. 7.\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also notched up its best one-week gain\par in five weeks, appreciating 0.45 percent over five straight\par days.\par     "State-run banks were buying for most of the day, both for\par customers and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and only after they let go did\par it end at a high of 43.5650," a trader at a state-run bank\par said.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has reined in the rupee since it scaled a\par five-year high of 43.30 in early February in order to keep\par local exports competitive and growing nearly as fast as the\par imports consumed by the liberalising and rapidly expanding\par economy.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts say concern about the high trade deficit, set to\par widen to record levels in this fiscal year ending March 31, is\par a key factor prompting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . This\par is, in turn, swelling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's pile of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves at a rapid\par pace.\par     India has the world's sixth-largest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reserves at $135.66 billion and comments by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par governor that the diversification of its holdings was being\par discussed fuelled market jitters worldwide over the U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakness.\par     The rupee has been benefitting from a tide of overseas\par portfolio investment, as investors expect annual economic\par growth of 7 percent to boost corporate earnings.\par     Foreign funds' net purchases of local shares are at more\par than $3 billion so far in 2005, which is more than a third of\par the record $8.5 billion they invested in stocks in 2004.\par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par     Bombay Sensitive Index\par     Indian rupee (/$)\par     7.38 percent 2015 bond (%)\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050311e13b008c1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
