\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee seen up on fund inflows into stocks.  \b0\par\par\uc2 392 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 03:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     BOMBAY, March 9 (Reuters) - The rupee is set to start\par higher on Wednesday, supported by rising foreign fund inflows\par into the booming stock market, dealers said.\par     "The dollar has fallen overseas and stocks are soaring so\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the rupee should add gains," a foreign bank dealer said. "We  \f28 \par \par \uc2 should see a test of 43.63 (per dollar) and one needs to see  \par \par \uc2 where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes in after that."  \par \par \uc2 In Asian trade, the dollar was near a two-month low against  \par \par \uc2 the euro , which was at $1.3340/41, on worries about the  \par \par \uc2 massive U.S. deficits and ahead of crucial trade data.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have been buying heavily into India's  \par \par \uc2 rallying stock market, which has scaled record peaks for the  \par \par \uc2 past four sessions.  \par \par \uc2 Their net purchases in just over two months of 2005 are at  \par \par \uc2 $2.56 billion, about a third of the record $8.5 billion they  \par \par \uc2 invested in 2004.  \par \par \uc2 But the Reserve Bank of India has kept the rupee on a tight  \par \par \uc2 leash since early February, when it hit a five-year peak of  \par \par \uc2 43.30, to help keep exports competitive.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee closed at 43.68/69 per dollar in thin  \par \par \uc2 trade on Tuesday at some centres like Calcutta and Bangalore.  \par \par \uc2 Banks in Bombay were closed for a local holiday.  \par \par \uc2 On Monday, the rupee ended little changed at 43.7300/7350  \par \par \uc2 in normal trade, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars to curb  \par \par \uc2 the rupee's gains.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has swelled  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to a record $135.66 billion,  \par \par \uc2 a near unprecedented increase of $5 billion over two weeks.  \par \par \uc2 "One cannot remember the last time we saw such sustained  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the foreign bank dealer said. "The  \par \par \uc2 only logic one can think of is that they must be keen to keep  \par \par \uc2 the REER (real effective exchange rate) within a 3 percent  \par \par \uc2 band."  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is keen to keep the rupee  \par \par \uc2 floating in an unofficial band of 3-5 percent against the  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of India's top five trading partners.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the latest surge in world oil prices  \par \par \uc2 to  \par \par \uc2 well past $54 per barrel would be watched closely, as oil is  \par \par \uc2 India's largest import.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par     Bombay Sensitive Index\par     Indian rupee (/$)\par     7.38 percent 2015 bond (%)\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050309e139001e5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
