\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee slips, nervous of  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 05:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, March 4 (Reuters) - The rupee was slightly weaker\par against the dollar early on Friday as expectations of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's gains outweighed\par talk of strong capital inflows and kept it largely range-bound.\par     At 10 a.m. (0430 GMT), the rupee          was at\par 43.7200/7250 per dollar, 0.03 percent weaker than its close at\par 43.70/71 on Thursday.\par     With the local share market at record highs, dealers\par expected strong investment inflows from foreign institutional\par investors (FIIs), which helped drive the rupee to an intraday\par high of 43.6350 per dollar on Thursday.\par  \par     "Every day it's flowing in from the FIIs. The rupee is\par holding because of the RBI," said a broker.\par     The Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (RBI) has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  regularly since mid-February to curb rupee appreciation in an   \par \par \uc2  effort to keep exports competitive. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a 5-year   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  just keeps buying dollars when (the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pair) goes to 43.65," said a dealer at a foreign bank.\par     "The market just doesn't know what to do."\par     The Bombay share index          crossed 6,800 to a new\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par record early on Friday as foreign funds stepped up purchases of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stocks after the government announced a pro-growth budget this\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign funds have bought more than $2.3 billion so far in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2005, compared with $8.5 billion for the whole of 2004. To see\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign funds data, please\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bankers say an initial public offering of India's biggest\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic airline, Jet Airways (India) Ltd., which closed last\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week, will draw in about $150 million of foreign inflows by\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par next Thursday.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But analysts say the RBI is keen to check the rupee, which\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par is allowed to float in an unofficial target band of 3-5 percent\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     JP Morgan estimates the rupee is overvalued by about 3\par percent on a trade-weighted basis .\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par     Bombay Sensitive Index\par     Indian rupee (/$)\par     7.38 percent 2015 bond (%)\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050304e13400296\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
