\par\par \b \uc2 India bonds edge up on official's borrowing comment.   \b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 13:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, March 2 (Reuters) - Indian bonds recovered a little\par ground on Wednesday after a top finance ministry official said\par the government's total borrowing in the next fiscal year may be\par less than budgeted, soothing concerns about a jump in\par issuances.\par     The yield on the benchmark 10-year bond\par   eased to 6.6286 percent from Tuesday's 6.6442\par percent, which was the highest close in more than three weeks.\par     The 10-year yield had surged 18 basis points in two days\par after the budget on Monday showed a sharply\par higher-than-expected borrowing plan to raise a net 1,038\par billion rupees in the year to March 2006, well above 940\par billion forecast in a Reuters poll.\par     Earlier on Wednesday, Economic Affairs Secretary Rakesh\par Mohan told reporters the borrowing plan was unlikely to put\par pressure on interest rates and said the total may be less than\par budgeted.\par  \par     "There is enough liquidity. Given the liquidity, one does\par not see problems in borrowing," Mohan said.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders said rising cash surpluses in the banking system,\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as reflected in the outstanding reverse repo balances and\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slowing inflation, had also helped to prop up shaky sentiment\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for now.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There is more than enough liquidity," a trader at a\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par state-run bank said. "With the RBI (Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 )\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continuously \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, it is only\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rising."\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been buying up most of the dollars\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par flowing into the country from overseas investors since February\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as it tries to cap the rupee's gains to keep exports\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par competitive.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupees released by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's dollar purchases\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par have in turn pushed up the amount parked at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short-term borrowing window to 441 billion rupees, the highest\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outstanding figure since March 29 last year.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Corporate bond yields were little changed in light trade\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par amid concerns over the borrowings plan. The yield on the\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters five-year benchmark bond  was steady at 7.02\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent, while its spread over a comparable federal bond rose a\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par basis point to 59. Its yield has risen 4 basis points since\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                           MARKET SNAPSHOT\par      Bombay Sensitive Index\par      Indian rupee (/$)\par      7.38 percent 2015 bond (%)\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050302e1320099k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
