\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee steady early, mkt eyes cbank, flows.  \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 05:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, March 2 (Reuters) - The rupee was steady early on\par Wednesday, supported by strong capital inflows but wary of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which has limited gains in recent\par weeks to keep exports competitive.\par     At 9:55 a.m. (0425 GMT), the rupee          was unchanged\par 43.7250/7350 per dollar, and dealers said they expected the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would trade in a range of 43.67-75.\par     Strong inflows of foreign capital into booming Bombay\par stocks would underpin the rupee, but dealers said they would\par wait for a key U.S. employment report, due out on Friday.\par Foreign funds have invested $2 billion in shares in the first\par two months of 2005.\par     "I think we'll wait for Friday. But, overall, sell the\par dollar on rallies," said a dealer at a foreign bank. "The fund\par flows are strong and the dollars are coming in."\par     Rallying shares drew in record foreign fund inflows of $8.5\par billion in 2005, lifting the rupee 5 percent last year.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  After\par modest flows in January, investments picked up in February and\par dealers say only the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is holding back the rupee.\par     The Indian government's pro-growth federal budget sent the\par benchmark Bombay share index  to record highs before a\par bout of profit-taking trimmed some gains.\par     The Indian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a five-year high of 43.30 per\par dollar in early February, but has since traded within a\par 43.50-43.80 range on sustained Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par  \par     Analysts say the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is keen to check the rupee,\par overvalued by about 3 percent on a trade-weighted basis.\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par     Bombay Sensitive Index\par     Indian rupee (/$)\par     7.38 percent 2015 bond (%)\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050302e13200461\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
