\par\par \b \uc2 India Markets-Shares off peak as oil cos slide, bonds tumble.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Suresh Seshadri   \par \uc2 604 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 14:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BOMBAY, March 1 (Reuters) - India's key share index slid back nearly 1 percent on Tuesday, after touching a record high, as investors cashed in on budget-led gains, while federal bonds slid to their lowest in more than three weeks on supply worries.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee ended slightly weaker as active \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains in check blunted the pro-growth federal budget's upward pressure on the unit.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 30-share Bombay index closed 0.94 percent lower at 6,651.08 points, after rallying to an all-time high of 6,725.92 points at the start. The previous high was 6,721.08 on Monday, when the index gained more than 2 percent.   \par \par \uc2 India's Congress-led coalition said in its 2005/06 (April-March) budget unveiled on Monday it would step up spending on infrastructure and the rural economy to spur growth and fight poverty. It also cut the corporate tax rate to 33 percent from 35.   \par \par \uc2 "Post-budget, we had a bit of euphoria in the market, and this has been a correction," said Sashi Krishnan, chief executive officer at Cholamandalam AMC Ltd.   \par \par \uc2 "It is nothing to get worried about at all. For a long-term investor, most budget proposals have little impact. A change of 2-3 percent in a company's profits will not impact your decision to invest in a fundamentally sound stock," Krishnan said.   \par \par \uc2 But a tax rejig for the energy sector is expected to increase losses for oil companies, already hurting from subsidies they provide on fuels like kerosene and cooking gas.   \par \par \uc2 State-run market leader Indian Oil Corp. Ltd. (IOC.BO) estimated oil companies would suffer additional losses of 4.5 billion rupees a month on higher excise duties on petrol and diesel, unless they were able to pass these on to the consumers.   \par \par \uc2 IOC's shares fell 4.76 percent, while shares of Bharat Petroleum Corp. Ltd. (BPCL.BO) fell 4.51 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Shares of UTI Bank (UTBK.BO) fell 6.2 percent after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new banking guidelines on Monday failed to raise the limit on foreign direct investment in private banks.   \par \par \uc2 Federal bonds tumbled as investors dumped debt over the government's plan to borrow a net 1.03 trillion rupees in the fiscal year starting in April, much higher than the 940 billion rupees forecast in a Reuters poll last month.   \par \par \uc2 The yield on the 10-year benchmark bond closed nearly 10 basis points higher at 6.6442 percent, taking the rise over the past two sessions to 18 basis points. It last closed higher at 6.7140 percent on Feb. 5.   \par \par \uc2 "The intended supply is ridiculously large and we could see monthly issuances jump by an additional about 60 billion rupees on average, which will see the curve surely steepening," a foreign bank trader said. The rupee surrendered most of the previous session's gains, losing 0.11 percent to close at 43.7250/7350 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee, which has been supported by capital inflows into the soaring stock market, firmed 0.13 percent on Monday after the budget, but dealers expect the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain in a broad 43.50-44.00 per dollar range in the next few sessions.   \par \par \uc2 The Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which set a five-year high of 43.30 per dollar in early February, has since drifted lower on sustained \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI), which analysts say is keen to ensure local exports remain competitive.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050301e13100b1w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
