\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee ends slightly weaker,cbank seen active.  \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 13:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, March 1 (Reuters) - The rupee ended slightly weaker\par on Tuesday, a day after a pro-growth federal budget that failed\par to give the market much direction because of active \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to limit the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's gains, dealers\par said.\par     The Indian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was stuck in a narrow range, gradually\par regaining early losses only to fall back at the close to end at\par 43.7250/7350 per dollar, down 0.1 percent from the previous\par close.\par     The rupee, which has been supported by capital inflows into\par the soaring stock market, firmed 0.13 percent on Monday after\par the budget, but dealers expected the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would\par remain in a broad 43.50-44.00 per dollar range.\par     One corporate trader said state-run banks that often act on\par behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were seen in the market again. "I\par think that we are going be stuck in this range for a while.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Neither is it going up nor is it going to come down."\par     Bombay shares closed at a record high on Monday after the\par government presented its budget for the coming fiscal year. The\par index climbed to an all-time high early on Tuesday, but\par retreated on profit-taking.\par     Rallying shares drew in record foreign fund inflows of $8.5\par billion in 2004, lifting the rupee 5 percent last year. Foreign\par funds bought $1.7 billion of Indian shares in Feb. 1-25, more\par than six times their investment in January, latest data showed.\par     The Indian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a five-year high of 43.30 per\par dollar in early February but has since drifted lower on\par sustained \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (RBI).\par  \par     Analysts say the RBI is keen to check the rupee, overvalued\par 3 percent on a trade-weighted basis.\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par     Bombay Sensitive Index\par     Indian rupee (/$)\par     7.38 percent 2015 bond (%)\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050301e131009qz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
