\par\par \b \uc2 Cbank trims gains in Indian rupee ahead of budget.  \b0\par\par\uc2 242 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2005\par 05:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Feb 28 (Reuters) - The rupee firmed early on\par Monday, eyeing the dollar's losses against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par but dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swiftly stepped in to temper\par the gains to keep exports competitive.\par     At 9:25 a.m. (0355 GMT), the rupee was at 43.64/65 per\par dollar, a fifth of a percent firmer than its close at\par 43.7250/7400 on Friday.\par     "It's because of the overseas dollar," said a trader at a\par foreign bank, adding that the market was also hoping that\par India's federal budget later in the day would also give them\par reasons to buy the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The dollar slipped against the yen following stronger than\par expected growth in Japan's industrial production in January and\par was also weaker against the euro , which traded around\par $1.3270.\par     But dealers said the Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (RBI), which has\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to limit the rupee's gains throughout much of\par February, was again seen buying dollars in early trade.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "The market tried to push it below the 43.66 level, but\par already the RBI is buying," the trader said.\par     India's 2005/06 federal budget, which is expected to boost\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investment in infrastructure and unveil tax reforms, will be\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par presented by Finance Minister Palaniappan Chidambaram at 11\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     To see what it may unveil, please\par                .\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par     Bombay Sensitive Index\par     Indian rupee (/$)\par     7.38 percent 2015 bond (%)\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050228e12s0033p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
