\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee seen steady early, awaits budget.  \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2005\par 04:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Feb 28 (Reuters) - The rupee is set to start steady\par on Monday, as traders await the Congress-led coalition's annual\par budget that is expected to give a boost to investment in\par infrastructure and unveil tax reforms.\par  \par     "Nobody is going to want to buy dollars at the moment given\par its weakness overseas," a senior dealer at a foreign bank said.\par     "But neither will people be selling it too aggressively\par till the budget is out and we have a clear picture of where the\par reforms and economy are headed in the coming year," he added.\par     Finance Minister Palaniappan Chidambaram will present the\par 2005/06 budget at 11:00 a.m. (0530 GMT). To see what it may\par unveil, please\par     "We should see the rupee in a 43.65-43.75 range till then,"\par the trading head at a private bank said.\par     In Asian trade, the dollar was broadly weaker fetching\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2  104.77/80 yen , and the euro  was at $1.3274/78.   \par \par \uc2  China's comments at the weekend that it will gradually open its   \par \par \uc2  capital account in 2005, in a step to full \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  convertibility, was weighing on sentiment in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  Traders said they would be watching for a possible upgrade   \par \par \uc2  of India's sovereign rating by global agencies, if the budget   \par \par \uc2  contained measures to reform the public finances.   \par \par \uc2  "An upgrade will really exert very strong pressure for the   \par \par \uc2  rupee to appreciate significantly," the foreign bank dealer   \par \par \uc2  said.   \par \par \uc2  Early gains could be muted by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,   \par \par \uc2  traders said. The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has held the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  on a tight leash over the past three weeks to keep exports   \par \par \uc2  competitive and prevent the trade deficit from widening   \par \par \uc2  sharply.   \par \par \uc2  "We need to see at what level state-run banks step in," the   \par \par \uc2  private bank trading head said. "Firm oil prices are still a   \par \par \uc2  concern."   \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the rupee  closed at 43.7250/7400 per   \par \par \uc2  dollar, sliding 0.10 percent from the previous session's   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par     Bombay Sensitive Index\par     Indian rupee (/$)\par     7.38 percent 2015 bond (%)\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050228e12s00262\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
