\par\par \b \uc2 India federal bonds recover as state-run banks buy.   \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2005\par 12:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Feb 22 (Reuters) - Indian federal bonds were firmer\par in afternoon trade on Tuesday, bouncing back from a weak start\par after strong purchases by state-run banks of the benchmark\par 10-year bond in a cash-flush market, dealers said.\par     The yield on the 10-year benchmark bond             eased\par to 6.4914 percent in fairly active trade from 6.5168 percent in\par the morning and compared with the previous close of 6.5042\par percent.\par  \par     "A state-run bank was buying hugely and that prompted\par others to buy," said a trader at a state-run bank.\par     Cash was in ample supply, as seen in the 215.35 billion\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rupees accepted at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's one-day reverse repo   \f28 \par \par \uc2 earlier Tuesday. The RBI accepted 136.95 billion rupees at   \par \par \uc2 Monday's reverse repo.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the ample liquidity, a result of the Reserve   \par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market,   \par \par \uc2 was lifting sentiment on bonds even as the marked cautiously   \par \par \uc2 watched NYMEX crude futures rise above $49 a barrel.   \par \par \uc2 Oil is India's biggest import item. While inflation has   \par \par \uc2 been easing in the past three months, a spike in oil prices   \par \par \uc2 last year lifted the rate to a 3-1/2-year peak in August,   \par \par \uc2 prompting the first monetary policy tightening in more than   \par \par \uc2 four years.   \par \par \uc2 Decent demand for a sale of state loans also boosted bonds,   \par \par \uc2 traders said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened the on-tap sale of 7.17   \par \par \uc2 percent 12-year loans for 16 state governments at 10:30 a.m.   \par \par \uc2 Results of the auction are expected in the evening.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "Once the subscription is over, there will be no new supply\par till March 31," the trader said.\par     The market is awaiting next Monday's federal budget to be\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 unveiled on Feb. 28 for cues. The benchmark 10-year bond is   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expected to trade around current levels before the budget,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 which will announce the government's borrowing programme for   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the fiscal year ahead.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Reuters poll of 10 fixed-income analysts showed a median   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 forecast for net borrowings for 2005/06 of 940 billion rupees,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 4 percent up from the 904 billion in the previous budget drawn   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 up in July after a change in government.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                           MARKET SNAPSHOT\par      Bombay Sensitive Index\par      Indian rupee (/$)\par      7.38 percent 2015 bond (%)\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050222e12m00ca3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
