\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee ends at 1-mth low, cbank seen selling.  \b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2005\par 13:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Feb 11 (Reuters) - The rupee slid to a one-month\par low on Friday as state-run banks bought dollars heavily for a\par fourth straight day, adding to market speculation that they\par were doing so on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Indian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  closed at 43.8250/8300 per dollar on\par Friday, its lowest close since Jan. 12 and down 0.1 percent\par from the previous day's close. The rupee traded at a low of\par 43.8350 shortly before the close, dealers said.\par  \par     "It was very clearly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  buying (dollars)," said a\par trader at a state-run bank.\par     The rupee has now shed 1.2 percent from last week's\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 five-year high of 43.30, set after global rating agency  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Standard & Poor's raised India's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could weaken yet further.  \par \par \uc2 "If the same level of aggression is there, we could see  \par \par \uc2 43.90 in two trading days," the trader said adding that the  \par \par \uc2 rupee could ease to 44 as early as next week.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee had firmed in early trade on Friday, after data  \par \par \uc2 showing a record U.S. trade deficit in 2004 halted the dollar's   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par six-week rally against the euro  and the yen       .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It soon retreated as state-run banks bought up dollars, as  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 they have for the past four sessions. The Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 often \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  via these banks to curb volatility and to keep  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the rupee competitive but rarely comments on its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  uses a monitoring band for the rupee that  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 allows the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to float within a 3 to 5 percent range  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of India's top five trading partners.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The data is published with a lag.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earlier in the week, JP Morgan Chase's real effective  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 exchange rate index showed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 overvalued by nearly 5 percent, and analysts said this could  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 have sparked off the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's dollar purchases.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The rupee was was still overvalued by nearly 4 percent on a\par trade-weighted basis, analysts said.\par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par     Bombay Sensitive Index\par     Indian rupee (/$)\par     7.38 percent 2015 bond (%)\par  -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050211e12b00bkr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
