\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee may recover as dlr halts, eyes cbank.  \b0\par\par\uc2 263 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2005\par 04:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Feb 11 (Reuters) - The rupee may recover from\par two-week lows as the dollar, weighed down by a record U.S.\par trade deficit, halted a six-week rally against major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but dealers will keep an eye out for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had gained early in the previous\par session\par  but slipped as state-run banks stepped up dollar purchases for\par the third straight day, possibly acting on behalf of the\par Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said.\par     The RBI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through state-run banks to curb\par excessive volatility in the market and to maintain the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's competitiveness but rarely comments on its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The rupee          ended at 43.77/78 per dollar on\par Thursday, its weakest since Jan. 27 and a shade softer than its\par previous close.\par     The rupee is still overvalued by about 4 percent on a\par trade-weighted basis, analysts said, adding this could have\par sparked off the latest bout of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The RBI uses a monitoring band for guiding the rupee in the\par medium term, which allows it to float within a 3 to 5 percent\par range determined by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of India's top five trading\par partners, but it publishes the data with a lag.\par     U.S. data showed the trade deficit in the world's largest\par economy surged to a record $617.7 billion in 2004, halting the\par dollar's six-week rally against the euro  and the yen\par  .\par  \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par     Bombay Sensitive Index\par     Indian rupee (/$)\par     7.38 percent 2015 bond (%)\par  -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050211e12b0035x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
