\par\par \b \uc2 RBI WATCH: India Moves To Correct Rupee Overvaluation  \b0\par\par\uc2 806 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2005\par 08:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Anil Varma \par  \par    A Dow Jones Newswires Column \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--Intensified \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caught the rupee market off guard this week, but the bank's move is hardly surprising as falling inflation now allows it to sterilize capital inflows without compromising on other policy aims.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 The Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which resumed heavy dollar buying this week after a gap of at least three months, is possibly seeking some downward correction in the overvalued rupee now to keep the country's burgeoning current account deficit within sustainable limits.  \par \par \uc2 The RBI's dollar buying has already pulled the rupee well below the 10-month peak scaled last week. Before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had risen steadily for weeks on strong stock-related capital inflows and broad dollar bearishness.  \par \par \uc2 At 0530 GMT, the dollar was at INR43.80, up from INR43.47 a week ago.  \par \par \uc2 Capital flows into the rallying Indian stock market topped $9 billion in 2004 - a record high. With inflows expected to stay strong this year, the RBI will likely continue siphoning out excess \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply to stress its well-known policy preferences - keeping the rupee fairly valued in trade-weighted terms and protecting export competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 "With the fall in inflation...and given the large current account deficit registered during July-September 2004, the RBI is more likely to use \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy to target competitiveness than inflation," said Barclays Capital in a recent research report.  \par \par \uc2 "The RBI is likely to believe that the most effective way, in the short run, of maintaining the current account deficit within sustainable limits, is by adjusting the rupee's real effective exchange rate," the report added. The real effective exchange rate, or REER, represents the rupee's value in trade-weighted terms.  \par \par \uc2 India's current account plunged into a $6.42 billion deficit in July-to-September 2004 from a $3.16 billion surplus in the previous quarter, mainly due to a sharp widening of the country's trade deficit. Its trade shortfall rose to $12.30 billion in July-September from $5.14 billion in the previous three months.  \par \par \uc2 Barclays suggested that the RBI probably made a "tactical retreat" by scaling back \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent months, for fear of swelling money supply that could aggravate inflationary pressures.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Lower Inflation To Help RBI \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indeed, persistently high inflation curbed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's ability to resist the rupee's rise through most of 2004. India's inflation hovered mostly close to multiyear highs in the second half of 2004 - it hit a 3 1/2-year high of 8.74% in August - mainly because of record high international oil prices.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, year-on-year inflation has moderated significantly since mid-December, falling to 5.25% by late January. Furthermore, inflation is expected to remain relatively moderate through 2005 due to a high statistical base.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This should give the RBI more elbowroom to sustain the stepped-up \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Siddharth Mathur, head of research at JP Morgan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , believes that the rupee's current overvaluation in trade terms is a dominant factor driving the RBI's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plan. The rupee's REER is currently around 104, indicating overvaluation - the rupee is considered fairly valued when its REER is 100.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The RBI may go slower on its dollar buying as the rupee's REER moves closer toward 100, he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The rupee's about close to 4% overvalued as of today. It's interesting to note that the rupee was even more overvalued - by almost 5% - on Tuesday, the day the RBI started buying dollars," said the treasury head at a local bank.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indeed, the rupee hasn't been allowed to become overvalued or undervalued in trade terms by more than 5% since the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crisis of 1997, noted Barclays Capital.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar's recent recovery against other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this week is one factor that has fed the rupee's current overvaluation. Several Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slipped this week as the dollar gained - the South Korean won by 1.2% and the Indonesian rupiah by 0.9% - but the rupee has lost only 0.6% so far, that too only because of the RBI's dollar buying.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Apart from the prospect of lower inflation, a recent slowing of India's export growth also may spur the RBI to sustain its dollar purchases. India's year-on-year export growth slowed to 14.6% in December 2004 from 26% in November and 43% in the year-ago period.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Anil Varma, Dow Jones Newswires, 91 22 22884212; anil.varma@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Anil Varma covers India's money and fixed income markets for Dow Jones Newswires)  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Madhu T in Mumbai contributed to this article)  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Costas Paris [ 11-02-05 0716GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1078 4282  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050211e12b0004s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
