\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee gives up gains, cbank cited-dealers.  \b0\par\par\uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2005\par 07:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Feb 10 (Reuters) - The rupee gave up early gains by\par mid-morning on Thursday as state-run banks, possibly acting on\par behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , stepped up dollar purchases in a\par bid to keep the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  competitive, dealers said.\par     At 11:40 a.m. (0610 GMT), the rupee          was quoted\par 43.8100/8200 per dollar, off 43.6950/7050 and down from the\par previous day's 43.7350/7450, which was the weakest close since\par Jan. 27.\par     "The state-run banks are buying dollars and we think it's\par probably engineered by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said a dealer at a\par foreign bank. "The dollar has risen recently against major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  probably wants the rupee to\par reflect that."\par     The rupee is still overvalued by about 4 percent on a\par trade-weighted basis, analysts said, adding this could have\par sparked off the latest bout of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupee, which is partially convertible, has now lost 0.7\par percent since the start of the week as the dollar gained\par overseas and after state-run banks bought dollars, amid growing\par talk they could be acting on behalf of the Reserve Bank of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (RBI).\par     The RBI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through state-run banks to curb\par excessive volatility in the market and to maintain the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's competitiveness.\par     The RBI uses a monitoring band for the guiding the rupee in\par the medium term, which allows it to float within a 3 to 5\par percent range determined by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of India's top five\par trading partners, but it publishes the data with a lag.\par  \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par     Bombay Sensitive Index\par     Indian rupee (/$)\par     7.38 percent 2015 bond (%)\par  -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050210e12a005k4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
